@startuml data-model-er
' Chapter 3, Software design, section 3.2: data model and persistence.
' Renders with any PlantUML processor, for example
' https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml or a local toolchain:
' plantuml docs/diagrams/data-model-er.puml
' Source of the facts shown here: app/src/main/java/de/miangohar/overload/
' data/local/entity, .../data/local/dao, .../data/local/Converters.kt,
' .../data/local/AppDatabase.kt, and docs/decision-log.md ADR-0003, ADR-0009.

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam entity {
  BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
  BorderColor #444444
  FontStyle normal
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #B8A000
}

title Overload, persisted data model (Room, database version 2)

entity "set_entries" as SetEntries {
  *id : INTEGER <<PK, autogenerate>>
  --
  date_epoch_day : INTEGER
  exercise_name : TEXT
  primary_muscle : TEXT
  secondary_muscles : TEXT
  sets : INTEGER
  reps : INTEGER
  weight_kg : REAL
  rir : INTEGER <<nullable>>
}

entity "training_goal" as TrainingGoal {
  *id : INTEGER <<PK, always 1>>
  --
  phase : TEXT
  block_length_weeks : INTEGER
  reminder_time : INTEGER <<nullable, added v2>>
}

entity "volume_targets" as VolumeTargets {
  *muscle_group : TEXT <<PK>>
  --
  min_sets : INTEGER
  max_sets : INTEGER
}

TrainingGoal .[#B8A000]. VolumeTargets : "no foreign key: a singleton goal,\ncleared and rewritten with its\ntargets in one transaction"

note bottom of SetEntries
  No relationship to the other two tables at the schema
  level. A week's totals are aggregated in Kotlin over
  plain queries, ADR-0009, not joined or grouped in SQL,
  so the rule stays unit testable off device.
end note

note as N1
  date_epoch_day: LocalDate stored as an epoch day, so
  rows can be ordered and range queried in SQL.
  primary_muscle, phase: enums stored by name.
  secondary_muscles: a Set<MuscleGroup> stored as one
  comma separated column.
  All four conversions live in Converters.kt.
end note
N1 .. SetEntries

note as N2
  DAOs return Flow, so a screen observing goal or
  entries updates itself on every write, no manual
  refresh call anywhere in the app.
end note
N2 .. TrainingGoal

note as N3
  Room, ADR-0003. Schema exported to app/schemas on
  every version bump; MIGRATION_1_2 (v1 to v2, adding
  reminder_time) is verified against the exported v1
  schema by AppDatabaseMigrationTest rather than
  written blind. The database itself is excluded from
  automatic cloud backup, ADR-0008.
end note
N3 .. VolumeTargets

@enduml
